<p>Thank you for your critique. The cowriter and I both agreed about the pronouns and I went and edited that. There is no real geological connection that I particularly thought about; those were Communism's additions and I liked them. In particular, I wanted the article to highlight the relation between the entity and a singular person. We aren't sure if everyone he contacts is drawn to subject B in this way, or if it is only subject A. But I wanted to imagine him as a brainwashed, love-addled servant, a priest to a deity he can only see when he closes his eyes.</p>
<p>I'm so happy I was able to convey the mystery, adoration, and overall unease I was after. I hoped that by keeping subject B mostly in the dark and providing only what the Foundation can see from without and what subject A can see from within, I could create in all of us a tiny, scant part that longs to serve as subject A does.</p>

